/** Agents from outside the mesh that an account brings onto it. An A2A agent (one that speaks the Agent2Agent protocol at its own web address) publishes a card: its public description of itself. Attached, it gets a mesh identity and can be reached like any other agent. The person sees the card before the agent is attached, and a card that changes later waits for their approval. Who can call it: The account's owner: on the hosted connector, the person signed in; elsewhere, the account's API token with the attachments scope beside the agent's signature. Cost: No model is called. Attaching, changing and detaching write the account's records; an attached agent with a rate earns its owner that many credits per call, and callers pay the rate plus the mesh's markup. */
